IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XVII, ss 206 and 206.1: COMPULSORY AND
-- COMPELLED ACQUISITIONS.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. After a take-over bid for all the shares of a class of a distributing corporation, an
-- offeror who has had at least 90 per cent accepted may buy out the holdouts ("dissenting offerees") by
-- sending a notice (s 206); a shareholder who never got that notice may require the offeror to buy them out
-- (s 206.1). The holdout either takes the bid's terms or demands "fair value" fixed by a court.
--
-- TIME. Periods are calendar days, each a `Time limit` of the keel: the day the period runs from is day 0
-- and the last day is that day plus the number of days (keel fork F1). "Not less than ninety per cent" is
-- written as 90% with a comparison that includes the boundary.
--
-- "Affiliate" and "associate" are the keel's (s 2); here they are the plain facts of what the offeror group
-- holds. Section 78 (notice of adverse claim) is piece cb2's; section 227(3) is in this piece
-- (cb4-after-dissolution).

§§ `s 206(1) Definitions`

-- src:2495 | Definitions
-- src:2496 | 206 (1) The definitions in this subsection apply in this Part.
-- src:2497 | dissenting offeree means, where a take-over bid is made for all the shares of a class of shares, a holder of a share of that class who does not accept the take-over bid and includes a subsequent holder of that share who acquires it from the first mentioned holder; (pollicité dissident)
@ref CBCA s 206(1) dissenting offeree (src:2497)
GIVEN `a take-over bid is made for all the shares of a class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a share of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has accepted the take-over bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a subsequent holder who acquired the share from a holder who has not accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is a dissenting offeree within s 206(1)` MEANS
        `a take-over bid is made for all the shares of a class`
    AND (    (    `the person holds a share of that class`
              AND (NOT `the person has accepted the take-over bid`))
         OR  `the person is a subsequent holder who acquired the share from a holder who has not accepted`)

-- "Offer includes an invitation to make an offer": an invitation is an offer. For anything else the
-- definition does not say.
-- src:2498 | offer includes an invitation to make an offer. (pollicitation)
@ref CBCA s 206(1) offer (src:2498)
GIVEN `the communication is an invitation to make an offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`whether a communication is an offer within s 206(1)` MEANS
    IF `the communication is an invitation to make an offer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2499 | offeree means a person to whom a take-over bid is made. (pollicité)
@ref CBCA s 206(1) offeree (src:2499)
GIVEN `a take-over bid is made to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is an offeree within s 206(1)` MEANS
    `a take-over bid is made to the person`

-- src:2500 | offeree corporation means a distributing corporation whose shares are the object of a take-over bid. (société pollicitée)
@ref CBCA s 206(1) offeree corporation (src:2500)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its shares are the object of a take-over bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a corporation is an offeree corporation within s 206(1)` MEANS
        `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
    AND `its shares are the object of a take-over bid`

-- src:2501 | offeror means a person, other than an agent or mandatary, who makes a take-over bid, and includes two or more persons who, directly or indirectly,
-- src:2502 | (a) make take-over bids jointly or in concert; or
-- src:2503 | (b) intend to exercise jointly or in concert voting rights attached to shares for which a take-over bid is made. (pollicitant)
@ref CBCA s 206(1) offeror (src:2501-2503)
GIVEN `the person makes a take-over bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an agent or mandatary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is one of two or more persons who, directly or indirectly, make take-over bids jointly or in concert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is one of two or more persons who, directly or indirectly, intend to exercise jointly or in concert voting rights attached to shares for which a take-over bid is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is an offeror within s 206(1)` MEANS
        (    `the person makes a take-over bid`
         AND (NOT `the person is an agent or mandatary`))
    OR  `the person is one of two or more persons who, directly or indirectly, make take-over bids jointly or in concert`
    OR  `the person is one of two or more persons who, directly or indirectly, intend to exercise jointly or in concert voting rights attached to shares for which a take-over bid is made`

-- "Share means a share, with or without voting rights, and includes (a) ... (b) ...": a closed meaning.
-- src:2504 | share means a share, with or without voting rights, and includes
-- src:2505 | (a) a security currently convertible into such a share; and
-- src:2506 | (b) currently exercisable options and rights to acquire such a share or such a convertible security. (action)
@ref CBCA s 206(1) share (src:2504-2506)
DECLARE `Kind of interest for the word share in s 206(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a share, with or without voting rights`
    `a security currently convertible into such a share (s 206(1) share (a))`
    `a currently exercisable option or right to acquire such a share or such a convertible security (s 206(1) share (b))`
    `an interest that is none of these`

@ref CBCA s 206(1) share (src:2504-2506)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of interest for the word share in s 206(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the interest is a share within s 206(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an interest that is none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:2507 | take-over bid means an offer made by an offeror to shareholders of a distributing corporation at approximately the same time to acquire all of the shares of a class of issued shares, and includes an offer made by a distributing corporation to repurchase all of the shares of a class of its shares. (offre d’achat visant à la mainmise)
@ref CBCA s 206(1) take-over bid (src:2507)
GIVEN `the offer is made by an offeror to shareholders of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made at approximately the same time to all of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to acquire all of the shares of a class of issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an offer by a distributing corporation to repurchase all of the shares of a class of its shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an offer is a take-over bid within s 206(1)` MEANS
        (    `the offer is made by an offeror to shareholders of a distributing corporation`
         AND `it is made at approximately the same time to all of them`
         AND `it is to acquire all of the shares of a class of issued shares`)
    OR  `it is an offer by a distributing corporation to repurchase all of the shares of a class of its shares`

§§ `s 206(2) and (3) The right to acquire, and the offeror's notice`

-- (2): acceptance within 120 days after the date of the bid by holders of not less than 90 per cent of the
-- shares of the class, leaving out shares the offeror or an affiliate or associate held at the date of the
-- bid. Three rules: when acceptances stop counting, whether one counts, and the 90 per cent test.
-- src:2508 | Right to acquire
-- src:2509 | (2) If within one hundred and twenty days after the date of a take-over bid the bid is accepted by the holders of not less than ninety per cent of the shares of any class of shares to which the take-over bid relates, other than shares held at the date of the take-over bid by or on behalf of the offeror or an affiliate or associate of the offeror, the offeror is entitled, on complying with this section, to acquire the shares held by the dissenting offerees.
@ref CBCA s 206(2) (src:2509)
GIVEN `the date of the take-over bid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for acceptances to count within s 206(2)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 120, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the date of the take-over bid`

@ref CBCA s 206(2) (src:2509)
GIVEN `the date of the take-over bid` IS A DATE
      `the day the acceptance was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the acceptance counts within s 206(2)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 120, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the date of the take-over bid` `the day the acceptance was received`

@ref CBCA s 206(2) (src:2509)
GIVEN `the number of shares of the class to which the bid relates` IS A NUMBER
      `the number held at the date of the bid by or on behalf of the offeror or an affiliate or associate of the offeror` IS A NUMBER
      `the number accepted in time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the bid has been accepted by not less than ninety per cent within s 206(2)` MEANS
    `the number accepted in time` AT LEAST (90%) TIMES (`the number of shares of the class to which the bid relates` MINUS `the number held at the date of the bid by or on behalf of the offeror or an affiliate or associate of the offeror`)

@ref CBCA s 206(2) (src:2509)
GIVEN `the bid has been accepted by not less than ninety per cent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror complies with section 206` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeror is entitled to acquire the shares held by the dissenting offerees within s 206(2)` MEANS
        `the bid has been accepted by not less than ninety per cent`
    AND `the offeror complies with section 206`

-- (3): the offeror's notice: registered mail, to each dissenting offeree and to the Director, within sixty
-- days after the date of termination of the bid AND within one hundred and eighty days after the date of the
-- bid (so by the earlier of the two last days), stating what (a) to (e) require.
-- src:2510 | Notice
-- src:2511 | (3) An offeror may acquire shares held by a dissenting offeree by sending by registered mail within sixty days after the date of termination of the take-over bid and in any event within one hundred and eighty days after the date of the take-over bid, an offeror’s notice to each dissenting offeree and to the Director stating that
@ref CBCA s 206(3) (src:2511)
GIVEN `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS A DATE
      `the date of the take-over bid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the offeror's notice within s 206(3)` MEANS
    `the earlier of two dates` (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 60, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the date of termination of the take-over bid`) (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 180, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the date of the take-over bid`)

@ref CBCA s 206(3) (src:2511)
GIVEN `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS A DATE
      `the date of the take-over bid` IS A DATE
      `the day the offeror sent the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeror's notice was sent in time within s 206(3)` MEANS
        `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 60, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the date of termination of the take-over bid` `the day the offeror sent the notice`
    AND `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 180, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the date of the take-over bid` `the day the offeror sent the notice`

-- src:2512 | (a) the offerees holding not less than ninety per cent of the shares to which the bid relates accepted the take-over bid;
-- src:2513 | (b) the offeror is bound to take up and pay for or has taken up and paid for the shares of the offerees who accepted the take-over bid;
-- src:2514 | (c) a dissenting offeree is required to elect
-- src:2515 | (i) to transfer their shares to the offeror on the terms on which the offeror acquired the shares of the offerees who accepted the take-over bid, or
-- src:2516 | (ii) to demand payment of the fair value of the shares in accordance with subsections (9) to (18) by notifying the offeror within twenty days after receiving the offeror’s notice;
-- src:2517 | (d) a dissenting offeree who does not notify the offeror in accordance with subparagraph (5)(b)(ii) is deemed to have elected to transfer the shares to the offeror on the same terms that the offeror acquired the shares from the offerees who accepted the take-over bid; and
-- src:2518 | (e) a dissenting offeree must send their shares to which the take-over bid relates to the offeree corporation within twenty days after receiving the offeror’s notice.
@ref CBCA s 206(3)(a), s 206(3)(b), s 206(3)(c), s 206(3)(d), s 206(3)(e) (src:2512 src:2513 src:2514 src:2517 src:2518)
GIVEN `it states that offerees holding not less than ninety per cent of the shares accepted the take-over bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the offeror is bound to take up and pay for, or has taken up and paid for, the shares of the offerees who accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that a dissenting offeree is required to elect to transfer the shares or to demand payment of fair value, by notifying the offeror within twenty days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that a dissenting offeree who does not so notify is deemed to have elected to transfer the shares on the same terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that a dissenting offeree must send the shares to the offeree corporation within twenty days after receiving the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeror's notice states what s 206(3) requires` MEANS
        `it states that offerees holding not less than ninety per cent of the shares accepted the take-over bid`
    AND `it states that the offeror is bound to take up and pay for, or has taken up and paid for, the shares of the offerees who accepted`
    AND `it states that a dissenting offeree is required to elect to transfer the shares or to demand payment of fair value, by notifying the offeror within twenty days`
    AND `it states that a dissenting offeree who does not so notify is deemed to have elected to transfer the shares on the same terms`
    AND `it states that a dissenting offeree must send the shares to the offeree corporation within twenty days after receiving the notice`

@ref CBCA s 206(3) (src:2511)
GIVEN `the notice was sent by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was sent to each dissenting offeree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was sent to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was sent in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states what section 206(3) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeror's notice complies with s 206(3)` MEANS
        `the notice was sent by registered mail`
    AND `it was sent to each dissenting offeree`
    AND `it was sent to the Director`
    AND `it was sent in time`
    AND `it states what section 206(3) requires`

§§ `s 206(4) to (8) What each side must do after the notice`

-- (4): the notice of adverse claim, concurrently, for each share held by a dissenting offeree. Section 78
-- (piece cb2) is a plain input.
-- src:2519 | Notice of adverse claim
-- src:2520 | (4) Concurrently with sending the offeror’s notice under subsection (3), the offeror shall send to the offeree corporation a notice of adverse claim in accordance with section 78 with respect to each share held by a dissenting offeree.
@ref CBCA s 206(4) (src:2520)
GIVEN `the offeror sends an offeror's notice under subsection 206(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeror must send the offeree corporation a notice of adverse claim for each share held by a dissenting offeree within s 206(4)` MEANS
    `the offeror sends an offeror's notice under subsection 206(3)`

@ref CBCA s 206(4) (src:2520)
GIVEN `it was sent concurrently with the offeror's notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 78 (piece cb2)
      `it is in accordance with section 78` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it covers each share held by a dissenting offeree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of adverse claim complies with s 206(4)` MEANS
        `it was sent concurrently with the offeror's notice`
    AND `it is in accordance with section 78`
    AND `it covers each share held by a dissenting offeree`

-- (5) and (5.1): twenty days from receiving the notice to send the certificates and to elect. If the
-- offeree does not notify the offeror of a demand for fair value in time, the offeree is DEEMED to have
-- elected to transfer on the same terms.
-- src:2521 | Share certificate
-- src:2522 | (5) A dissenting offeree to whom an offeror’s notice is sent under subsection (3) shall, within twenty days after receiving the notice,
-- src:2523 | (a) send the share certificates of the class of shares to which the take-over bid relates to the offeree corporation; and
-- src:2524 | (b) elect
-- src:2525 | (i) to transfer the shares to the offeror on the terms on which the offeror acquired the shares of the offerees who accepted the take-over bid, or
-- src:2526 | (ii) to demand payment of the fair value of the shares in accordance with subsections (9) to (18) by notifying the offeror within those twenty days.
@ref CBCA s 206(5) (src:2522-2526)
GIVEN `the day the dissenting offeree received the offeror's notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the dissenting offeree to send the certificates and elect within s 206(5)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the dissenting offeree received the offeror's notice`

@ref CBCA s 206(5) (src:2522-2523)
GIVEN `the day the dissenting offeree received the offeror's notice` IS A DATE
      `the day the dissenting offeree sent the share certificates` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certificates were sent in time within s 206(5)(a)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the dissenting offeree received the offeror's notice` `the day the dissenting offeree sent the share certificates`

-- src:2527 | Deemed election
-- src:2528 | (5.1) A dissenting offeree who does not notify the offeror in accordance with subparagraph (5)(b)(ii) is deemed to have elected to transfer the shares to the offeror on the same terms on which the offeror acquired the shares from the offerees who accepted the take-over bid.
DECLARE `Election of a dissenting offeree under s 206(5)` IS ONE OF
    `to transfer the shares on the terms on which the offeror acquired the shares of the offerees who accepted`
    `to demand payment of the fair value of the shares`

@ref CBCA s 206(5), s 206(5.1) (src:2524-2526 src:2528)
GIVEN `the offeree notified the offeror of a demand for payment of fair value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the dissenting offeree received the offeror's notice` IS A DATE
      `the day the offeree notified the offeror` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Election of a dissenting offeree under s 206(5)`
`the election of the dissenting offeree within s 206(5) and s 206(5.1)` MEANS
    IF     `the offeree notified the offeror of a demand for payment of fair value`
       AND `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the dissenting offeree received the offeror's notice` `the day the offeree notified the offeror`
    THEN `to demand payment of the fair value of the shares`
    ELSE `to transfer the shares on the terms on which the offeror acquired the shares of the offerees who accepted`

-- (6): twenty days after the offeror sends the notice, the offeror pays or transfers to the offeree
-- corporation what a dissenting offeree electing to transfer would be owed.
-- src:2529 | Payment
-- src:2530 | (6) Within twenty days after the offeror sends an offeror’s notice under subsection (3), the offeror shall pay or transfer to the offeree corporation the amount of money or other consideration that the offeror would have had to pay or transfer to a dissenting offeree if the dissenting offeree had elected to accept the take-over bid under subparagraph (5)(b)(i).
@ref CBCA s 206(6) (src:2530)
GIVEN `the day the offeror sent the notice under subsection 206(3)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the offeror to pay or transfer to the offeree corporation within s 206(6)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the offeror sent the notice under subsection 206(3)`

@ref CBCA s 206(6) (src:2530)
GIVEN `the day the offeror sent the notice under subsection 206(3)` IS A DATE
      `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeror paid or transferred in time within s 206(6)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the offeror sent the notice under subsection 206(3)` `the day the offeror paid or transferred`

-- (7) and (7.1): trust, separate account, insured bank.
-- src:2531 | Consideration
-- src:2532 | (7) The offeree corporation is deemed to hold in trust for the dissenting shareholders the money or other consideration it receives under subsection (6), and the offeree corporation shall deposit the money in a separate account in a bank or other body corporate any of whose deposits are insured by the Canada Deposit Insurance Corporation or guaranteed by the Quebec Deposit Insurance Board, and shall place the other consideration in the custody of a bank or such other body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 206(7) (src:2532)
GIVEN `the offeree corporation has received money or other consideration under subsection 206(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeree corporation holds the money or consideration in trust for the dissenting shareholders within s 206(7)` MEANS
    `the offeree corporation has received money or other consideration under subsection 206(6)`

@ref CBCA s 206(7) (src:2532)
GIVEN `the money is deposited in a separate account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the account is in a bank or other body corporate whose deposits are insured by the Canada Deposit Insurance Corporation or guaranteed by the Quebec Deposit Insurance Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other consideration is placed in the custody of a bank or such other body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the deposit and custody comply with s 206(7)` MEANS
        `the money is deposited in a separate account`
    AND `the account is in a bank or other body corporate whose deposits are insured by the Canada Deposit Insurance Corporation or guaranteed by the Quebec Deposit Insurance Board`
    AND `any other consideration is placed in the custody of a bank or such other body corporate`

-- src:2533 | When corporation is offeror
-- src:2534 | (7.1) A corporation that is an offeror making a take-over bid to repurchase all of the shares of a class of its shares is deemed to hold in trust for the dissenting shareholders the money and other consideration that it would have had to pay or transfer to a dissenting offeree if the dissenting offeree had elected to accept the take-over bid under subparagraph (5)(b)(i), and the corporation shall, within twenty days after a notice is sent under subsection (3), deposit the money in a separate account in a bank or other body corporate any of whose deposits are insured by the Canada Deposit Insurance Corporation or guaranteed by the Quebec Deposit Insurance Board, and shall place the other consideration in the custody of a bank or such other body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 206(7.1) (src:2534)
GIVEN `the corporation is an offeror making a take-over bid to repurchase all the shares of a class of its shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation holds the money and consideration in trust for the dissenting shareholders within s 206(7.1)` MEANS
    `the corporation is an offeror making a take-over bid to repurchase all the shares of a class of its shares`

@ref CBCA s 206(7.1) (src:2534)
GIVEN `the day a notice was sent under subsection 206(3)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the corporation to deposit the money within s 206(7.1)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day a notice was sent under subsection 206(3)`

@ref CBCA s 206(7.1) (src:2534)
GIVEN `the day a notice was sent under subsection 206(3)` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation deposited the money` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation deposited in time within s 206(7.1)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day a notice was sent under subsection 206(3)` `the day the corporation deposited the money`

-- (8): within thirty days after the offeror sends the notice, the offeree corporation does three things,
-- each on its own conditions.
-- src:2535 | Duty of offeree corporation
-- src:2536 | (8) Within thirty days after the offeror sends a notice under subsection (3), the offeree corporation shall
@ref CBCA s 206(8) (src:2536)
GIVEN `the day the offeror sent the notice under subsection 206(3)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the offeree corporation to act within s 206(8)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the offeror sent the notice under subsection 206(3)`

@ref CBCA s 206(8) (src:2536)
GIVEN `the day the offeror sent the notice under subsection 206(3)` IS A DATE
      `the day the offeree corporation acted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeree corporation acted in time within s 206(8)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the offeror sent the notice under subsection 206(3)` `the day the offeree corporation acted`

-- src:2537 | (a) if the payment or transfer required by subsection (6) is made, issue to the offeror a share certificate in respect of the shares that were held by dissenting offerees;
@ref CBCA s 206(8)(a) (src:2537)
GIVEN `the payment or transfer required by subsection 206(6) is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeree corporation must issue the offeror a share certificate within s 206(8)(a)` MEANS
    `the payment or transfer required by subsection 206(6) is made`

-- src:2538 | (b) give to each dissenting offeree who elects to accept the take-over bid terms under subparagraph (5)(b)(i) and who sends share certificates as required by paragraph (5)(a) the money or other consideration to which the offeree is entitled, disregarding fractional shares, which may be paid for in money; and
@ref CBCA s 206(8)(b) (src:2538)
GIVEN `the dissenting offeree elected to accept the take-over bid terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dissenting offeree sent the share certificates as required by paragraph 206(5)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeree corporation must give the dissenting offeree the money or consideration within s 206(8)(b)` MEANS
        `the dissenting offeree elected to accept the take-over bid terms`
    AND `the dissenting offeree sent the share certificates as required by paragraph 206(5)(a)`

-- src:2539 | (c) if the payment or transfer required by subsection (6) is made and the money or other consideration is deposited as required by subsection (7) or (7.1), send to each dissenting shareholder who has not sent share certificates as required by paragraph (5)(a) a notice stating that
-- src:2540 | (i) the dissenting shareholder’s shares have been cancelled,
-- src:2541 | (ii) the offeree corporation or some designated person holds in trust for the dissenting shareholder the money or other consideration to which that shareholder is entitled as payment for or in exchange for the shares, and
-- src:2542 | (iii) the offeree corporation will, subject to subsections (9) to (18), send that money or other consideration to that shareholder without delay after receiving the shares.
@ref CBCA s 206(8)(c) (src:2539-2542)
GIVEN `the payment or transfer required by subsection 206(6) is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money or other consideration is deposited as required by subsection 206(7) or 206(7.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dissenting shareholder has not sent share certificates as required by paragraph 206(5)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeree corporation must send the dissenting shareholder the notice within s 206(8)(c)` MEANS
        `the payment or transfer required by subsection 206(6) is made`
    AND `the money or other consideration is deposited as required by subsection 206(7) or 206(7.1)`
    AND `the dissenting shareholder has not sent share certificates as required by paragraph 206(5)(a)`

@ref CBCA s 206(8)(c) (src:2540-2542)
GIVEN `it states that the shares have been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the offeree corporation or a designated person holds the money or consideration in trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the offeree corporation will send it without delay after receiving the shares, subject to subsections 206(9) to 206(18)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeree corporation's notice states what s 206(8)(c) requires` MEANS
        `it states that the shares have been cancelled`
    AND `it states that the offeree corporation or a designated person holds the money or consideration in trust`
    AND `it states that the offeree corporation will send it without delay after receiving the shares, subject to subsections 206(9) to 206(18)`

§§ `s 206(9) to (18) The court`

-- (9): the offeror may apply within twenty days after paying or transferring under (6).
-- src:2543 | Application to court
-- src:2544 | (9) If a dissenting offeree has elected to demand payment of the fair value of the shares under subparagraph (5)(b)(ii), the offeror may, within twenty days after it has paid the money or transferred the other consideration under subsection (6), apply to a court to fix the fair value of the shares of that dissenting offeree.
@ref CBCA s 206(9) (src:2544)
GIVEN `the dissenting offeree has elected to demand payment of the fair value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the offeror paid or transferred under subsection 206(6)` IS A DATE
      `the day the offeror applied to the court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeror may apply to a court to fix the fair value within s 206(9)` MEANS
        `the dissenting offeree has elected to demand payment of the fair value`
    AND `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the offeror paid or transferred under subsection 206(6)` `the day the offeror applied to the court`

@ref CBCA s 206(9) (src:2544)
GIVEN `the day the offeror paid or transferred under subsection 206(6)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the offeror to apply to a court within s 206(9)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the offeror paid or transferred under subsection 206(6)`

-- (10): if the offeror fails to apply, the dissenting offeree may apply within a FURTHER twenty days (fork
-- F4, as for s 190(16): the further twenty days follow the end of the offeror's twenty).
-- src:2545 | Idem
-- src:2546 | (10) If an offeror fails to apply to a court under subsection (9), a dissenting offeree may apply to a court for the same purpose within a further period of twenty days.
@ref CBCA s 206(10) (src:2546)
GIVEN `the offeror failed to apply to a court under subsection 206(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the offeror paid or transferred under subsection 206(6)` IS A DATE
      `the day the dissenting offeree applied to the court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dissenting offeree may apply to a court to fix the fair value within s 206(10)` MEANS
        `the offeror failed to apply to a court under subsection 206(9)`
    AND `the day the dissenting offeree applied to the court` GREATER THAN (`the last day for the offeror to apply to a court within s 206(9)` `the day the offeror paid or transferred under subsection 206(6)`)
    AND `the day the dissenting offeree applied to the court` AT MOST (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` (`the last day for the offeror to apply to a court within s 206(9)` `the day the offeror paid or transferred under subsection 206(6)`))

@ref CBCA s 206(10) (src:2546)
GIVEN `the day the offeror paid or transferred under subsection 206(6)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the dissenting offeree to apply to a court within s 206(10)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` (`the last day for the offeror to apply to a court within s 206(9)` `the day the offeror paid or transferred under subsection 206(6)`)

-- (11): no application under (10) in that period: deemed election to transfer on the same terms.
-- src:2547 | Status of dissenter if no court application
-- src:2548 | (11) Where no application is made to a court under subsection (10) within the period set out in that subsection, a dissenting offeree is deemed to have elected to transfer their shares to the offeror on the same terms that the offeror acquired the shares from the offerees who accepted the take-over bid.
@ref CBCA s 206(11) (src:2548)
GIVEN `no application was made to a court under subsection 206(10) within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Election of a dissenting offeree under s 206(5)`
`the deemed election within s 206(11)` MEANS
    IF `no application was made to a court under subsection 206(10) within the period`
    THEN JUST `to transfer the shares on the terms on which the offeror acquired the shares of the offerees who accepted`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (12): the venue, as in s 190(17).
-- src:2549 | Venue
-- src:2550 | (12) An application under subsection (9) or (10) shall be made to a court having jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office or in the province where the dissenting offeree resides if the corporation carries on business in that province.
@ref CBCA s 206(12) (src:2550)
GIVEN `the court has jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has jurisdiction in the province where the dissenting offeree resides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation carries on business in that province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court is a proper court within s 206(12)` MEANS
        `the court has jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office`
    OR  (    `the court has jurisdiction in the province where the dissenting offeree resides`
         AND `the corporation carries on business in that province`)

-- src:2551 | No security for costs
-- src:2552 | (13) A dissenting offeree is not required to give security for costs in an application made under subsection (9) or (10).
@ref CBCA s 206(13) (src:2552)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection 206(9) or 206(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a dissenting offeree is required to give security for costs within s 206(13)` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under subsection 206(9) or 206(10)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2553 | Parties
-- src:2554 | (14) On an application under subsection (9) or (10)
-- src:2555 | (a) all dissenting offerees referred to in subparagraph (5)(b)(ii) whose shares have not been acquired by the offeror shall be joined as parties and are bound by the decision of the court; and
-- src:2556 | (b) the offeror shall notify each affected dissenting offeree of the date, place and consequences of the application and of their right to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 206(14)(a) (src:2555)
GIVEN `the dissenting offeree elected under subparagraph 206(5)(b)(ii) and the offeror has not acquired the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dissenting offeree must be joined as a party and is bound by the decision within s 206(14)(a)` MEANS
    `the dissenting offeree elected under subparagraph 206(5)(b)(ii) and the offeror has not acquired the shares`

@ref CBCA s 206(14)(b) (src:2556)
GIVEN `the notice states the date of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the place of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the consequences of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the right to appear and be heard in person or by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeror's notice to the dissenting offeree complies with s 206(14)(b)` MEANS
        `the notice states the date of the application`
    AND `the notice states the place of the application`
    AND `the notice states the consequences of the application`
    AND `the notice states the right to appear and be heard in person or by counsel`

-- src:2557 | Powers of court
-- src:2558 | (15) On an application to a court under subsection (9) or (10), the court may determine whether any other person is a dissenting offeree who should be joined as a party, and the court shall then fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting offerees.
@ref CBCA s 206(15) (src:2558)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 206(9) or 206(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court must fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting offerees within s 206(15)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 206(9) or 206(10)`

-- src:2559 | Appraisers
-- src:2560 | (16) A court may in its discretion appoint one or more appraisers to assist the court to fix a fair value for the shares of a dissenting offeree.
@ref CBCA s 206(16) (src:2560)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 206(9) or 206(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may appoint appraisers within s 206(16)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 206(9) or 206(10)`

-- src:2561 | Final order
-- src:2562 | (17) The final order of the court shall be made against the offeror in favour of each dissenting offeree and for the amount for the shares as fixed by the court.
@ref CBCA s 206(17) (src:2562)
GIVEN `the court has fixed a fair value for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the final order is made against the offeror in favour of each dissenting offeree within s 206(17)` MEANS
    `the court has fixed a fair value for the shares`

-- (18): any order it thinks fit, including four named. The interest runs from the day the dissenting
-- offeree sends or delivers the certificates under (5) until the day of payment, both included.
-- src:2563 | Additional powers
-- src:2564 | (18) In connection with proceedings under this section, a court may make any order it thinks fit and, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, it may
-- src:2565 | (a) fix the amount of money or other consideration that is required to be held in trust under subsection (7) or (7.1);
-- src:2566 | (b) order that that money or other consideration be held in trust by a person other than the offeree corporation;
-- src:2567 | (c) allow a reasonable rate of interest on the amount payable to each dissenting offeree from the date they send or deliver their share certificates under subsection (5) until the date of payment; and
-- src:2568 | (d) order that any money payable to a shareholder who cannot be found be paid to the Receiver General and subsection 227(3) applies in respect thereof.
@ref CBCA s 206(18) (src:2564-2568)
DECLARE `Kind of order under s 206(18)` IS ONE OF
    `an order fixing the amount of money or other consideration required to be held in trust under subsection (7) or (7.1) (s 206(18)(a))`
    `an order that the money or other consideration be held in trust by a person other than the offeree corporation (s 206(18)(b))`
    `an order allowing a reasonable rate of interest on the amount payable to each dissenting offeree (s 206(18)(c))`
    `an order that money payable to a shareholder who cannot be found be paid to the Receiver General, with subsection 227(3) applying (s 206(18)(d))`
    `any other order the court thinks fit under s 206(18)`

@ref CBCA s 206(18) (src:2564-2568)
GIVEN `the court thinks the order fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made in connection with proceedings under section 206` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of order under s 206(18)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make the order within s 206(18)` MEANS
        `the court thinks the order fit`
    AND `the order is made in connection with proceedings under section 206`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `an order fixing the amount of money or other consideration required to be held in trust under subsection (7) or (7.1) (s 206(18)(a))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an order that the money or other consideration be held in trust by a person other than the offeree corporation (s 206(18)(b))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an order allowing a reasonable rate of interest on the amount payable to each dissenting offeree (s 206(18)(c))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an order that money payable to a shareholder who cannot be found be paid to the Receiver General, with subsection 227(3) applying (s 206(18)(d))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `any other order the court thinks fit under s 206(18)` THEN TRUE)

@ref CBCA s 206(18)(c) (src:2567)
GIVEN `the day the dissenting offeree sent or delivered the share certificates under subsection 206(5)` IS A DATE
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may allow interest for a day within s 206(18)(c)` MEANS
        `the day I am asking about` AT LEAST `the day the dissenting offeree sent or delivered the share certificates under subsection 206(5)`
    AND `the day I am asking about` AT MOST `the day of payment`

§§ `s 206.1 Obligation to acquire shares`

-- (1): a shareholder who did not receive the offeror's notice may require the offeror to buy them out: within
-- ninety days after termination of the bid or, if the shareholder never received an offer, within ninety days
-- after the later of termination and the day the shareholder learned of the bid.
-- src:2569 | Obligation to acquire shares
-- src:2570 | 206.1 (1) If a shareholder holding shares of a distributing corporation does not receive an offeror’s notice under subsection 206(3), the shareholder may
-- src:2571 | (a) within ninety days after the date of termination of the take-over bid, or
-- src:2572 | (b) if the shareholder did not receive an offer pursuant to the take-over bid, within ninety days after the later of
-- src:2573 | (i) the date of termination of the take-over bid, and
-- src:2574 | (ii) the date on which the shareholder learned of the take-over bid,
-- src:2575 | require the offeror to acquire those shares.
@ref CBCA s 206.1(1) (src:2570-2575)
GIVEN `the shareholder received an offer pursuant to the take-over bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS A DATE
      `the day the shareholder learned of the take-over bid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the ninety days for the shareholder start within s 206.1(1)` MEANS
    IF `the shareholder received an offer pursuant to the take-over bid`
    THEN `the date of termination of the take-over bid`
    ELSE `the later of two dates` `the date of termination of the take-over bid` `the day the shareholder learned of the take-over bid`

@ref CBCA s 206.1(1) (src:2570-2575)
GIVEN `the day the ninety days start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the shareholder to require the offeror to acquire within s 206.1(1)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 90, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the ninety days start`

@ref CBCA s 206.1(1) (src:2570-2575)
GIVEN `the shareholder holds shares of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder did not receive an offeror's notice under subsection 206(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the ninety days start` IS A DATE
      `the day the shareholder required the offeror to acquire the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder may require the offeror to acquire the shares within s 206.1(1)` MEANS
        `the shareholder holds shares of a distributing corporation`
    AND `the shareholder did not receive an offeror's notice under subsection 206(3)`
    AND `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 90, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the ninety days start` `the day the shareholder required the offeror to acquire the shares`

-- src:2576 | Conditions
-- src:2577 | (2) If a shareholder requires the offeror to acquire shares under subsection (1), the offeror shall acquire the shares on the same terms under which the offeror acquired or will acquire the shares of the offerees who accepted the take-over bid.
@ref CBCA s 206.1(2) (src:2577)
GIVEN `a shareholder has required the offeror to acquire shares under subsection 206.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offeror must acquire the shares on the same terms as the offerees who accepted within s 206.1(2)` MEANS
    `a shareholder has required the offeror to acquire shares under subsection 206.1(1)`
